From dbcfa02bda32f7f2e194eea995a70ac625e54922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:14:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/38] feat(qsa): host-resident full-attention K/V (UVA
 zero-copy) + GPU hot cache

SGLANG_QSA_HOST_KV=target|all keeps QSA full-attention K/V in pinned,
device-mapped host memory; compressed indexer keys stay on GPU. Existing
gather/store kernels read/write it through UVA. Pool sizing charges only
GPU-resident bytes. Direct-mapped per-(layer,request) GPU hot cache at
compressed-group granularity absorbs repeated selections (SGLANG_QSA_HOST_KV_CACHE_SETS).
